Licenses for the thesis reproduction materials
==============================================

The new reproduction tools and documentation listed in
LICENSE_SCOPE.md are licensed under the MIT License. Their notice
identifies the contributors to the thesis reproduction tools. This
includes the root launcher, user guides and listed HIL verification
scripts; it does not include the data processed by those scripts.

Guoqing Lu also offers the portions of the historical research software
that he authored and is entitled to license under MIT. His notice applies
to those contributions only.

See MIT.txt for the license text and notices and
LICENSE_SCOPE.md for the exact files and exceptions. Retain the MIT
copyright and permission notices in copies or substantial portions
of the covered works. There is no blanket license over the historical source trees or project records;
Intel Lab inputs and external dependencies have their own terms.

Inside the downloadable package, the same license text and scope are in
legal/MIT.txt and legal/LICENSE_SCOPE.md. The download-page
README, its overview illustration, and the root archive launcher, pinned
requirements and checksums are reproduction tools and documentation under
the contributor MIT notice. The terms for the contents of the study archive
are unchanged.
